ive because I'm  sure they've probably tried to petition  the government I'm sure they try to  reach out to local officials and hold  protests if not about this Confederate  statue in particular about other ones  we've seen that all across the country  and so many of them are still up there  still standing right now so if you have  actually people who are willing to tear  them down at themselves and then  spray-paint them and get it to a point  where it's a risk to even have that  monument there because it attracts  protesters and it's risks to public  safety and public health and all that  maybe that is the move maybe that is the  right thing to do and we could be seeing  it before our very eyes last thing just  like a disclaimer I think Pat and I both  realize Confederate statues are not the  most important thing going on right now  and we have much bigger problems to  solve and whether the statues stay up or  come down it doesn't fix the broader  issues we're dealing with but it's an  interesting discussion and one that has  been the subject of a lot of different  articles over the last 24 hours so I  think it is worth worth spitballing at  some  ideas about that's going to do it for  today I hope you'll join us tomorrow  we've got a new show and the new bonus  show both are coming up tomorrow the  david pakman show at david pakman.com  [Music]
 

